** Bench G: the Fig. 15 comparator on its own, driven through the node impedance of the summing stage.
** Needs comparator.spice (or your own subcircuit with the same pins) in the same folder. 250 cycles of 100 ns (full plan), corner tt, 27 C.
** Cycle k starts at k*100 ns: reset (phi1 LOW = T9 on, phi2 HIGH = NMOS latch off and Q = Qb = 0), the inputs step at +2 ns,
**   phi1 rises at +70 ns (release, PMOS latch regenerates), phi2 falls at +72 ns (gap 2 ns, NMOS latch connected),
**   at the end of the cycle phi2 rises at 100 ns and phi1 falls 0.3 ns later (reset again, the decision is lost on Q/Qb).
** Groups: A = overdrive 0.1..100 mV both signs; B = common mode 0.6..1.3 V at +/-5 mV and +/-1 mV (full plan only); C = offset ramp, up then down.
** An SR latch (two NOR gates) on Q/Qb holds the decision through the reset: outputs vlat / vlatb.
** Generated by make_benchG.py.
.include comparator.spice

.param rsrc=35000 cin=9.5e-14 cout=1e-14
